<p>Reports the <code>value</code> / <code>expression</code> attribute of the Spring test annotations
<a href="https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/current/javadoc-api/org/springframework/test/context/junit/jupiter/EnabledIf.html">@EnabledIf</a>
and <code>@DisabledIf</code> when it is a plain literal that cannot evaluate to a boolean at runtime.</p>

<p>The attribute must be a SpEL expression (<code>#{...}</code>), a property placeholder (<code>${...}</code>),
or the literal <code>true</code> / <code>false</code>.</p>

<p><b>Example:</b></p>
<pre><code lang="java">
  @Test
  @EnabledIf("yes") // reports: not a SpEL expression, placeholder, or 'true'/'false'
  void test() {...}

  @Test
  @EnabledIf("#{@conditionService.isConditionMet}") // ok
  void spelTest() {...}

  @Test
  @EnabledIf("${my.props.condition:true}") // ok
  void propertyTest() {...}
</code></pre>
</body>
